ift"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Posterior"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Beta × Beta"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Policy"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Constrained TS"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Evidence"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Randomized holdout"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"_paper_s3c3x_37","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"_chapter_s3c3x_13","id":"system","aria-labelledby":"system-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"_chapterLabel_s3c3x_41","children":"01 / System"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"_chapterBody_s3c3x_43","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"_chapterHead_s3c3x_13","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Chapter one · identification and segmentation"}],["$","h2",null,{"id":"system-title","children":"A response model is not a treatment policy."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The estimand, the split rule, and the economic action must refer to the same pre-treatment population."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"_proseGrid_s3c3x_51","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Potential outcomes"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["For unit ",["$","em",null,{"children":"i"}],", let Yᵢ(1) and Yᵢ(0) be conversion under assigned treatment and control. Only Yᵢ=ZᵢYᵢ(1)+(1−Zᵢ)Yᵢ(0) is observed. Random assignment gives conditional exchangeability; consistency connects assignment to the observed outcome, no interference fixes each unit’s outcome against other assignments, and positivity requires 0<P(Z=1|X=x)<1 wherever a policy may act. Under these conditions, the conditional average treatment effect is identified."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Assignment is not exposure"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Z is the randomized treatment assignment. A downstream impression or click is post-treatment exposure E(Z), so conditioning on E=1 selects a treatment-affected population and can open collider bias. The policy therefore learns intent-to-treat uplift from randomized assignment, while exposure enters only as an operational cost or separately randomized mechanism."}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"_formula_s3c3x_61","children":["$L7","$L8","$L9"]}],"$La","$Lb","$Lc"]}]]}],"$Ld","$Le","$Lf"]}]]}],"$L10"]}]]
