mpled net value first. A global budget bounds total treatment; a segment-share cap prevents one leaf from absorbing all supply. Arm-specific precision targets imply a lower treatment count and a control-reserve upper bound in each leaf. Infeasible or posterior-gated leaves receive zero; unused budget remains explicit."}]]}]]}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"_formula_s3c3x_61","children":[["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"Posterior gate and sampled objective"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"math-render","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$18"}}],"$L19"]}],"$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e"]}]]}]
